1,0 $ ===> RETOUR AU KIT $$f"Conocybe_kit.cle"
1,0,$
1,0 $ Lamellae mature dark brown, spore print violaceous brown, spores in KOH chocolate $$s"Sect. Conocybella"
1,0,N$/// Sect. Conocybella (extra-European) 
1,2 $ Lamellae mature brownish yellow, yellow- to rubiginous; spore print mostly yellow-brown to rubiginous, rarely brownish yellow or dark brown; spores in KOH yellow, rubiginous to reddish brown, rarely hyaline 

2,cs6 $ Basidiocarp large, with Tricholoma-habit, reminding of a Hebeloma; pileus up to 80 mm wide, stipe up to 80 x 15 mm $$s"Sect. Giganteae"
2,3 $ Basidiocarp small to medium, with Mycena-habit; pileus mostly much smaller, if large then stipe slenderer and thinner

3,cs7 $ Spore surface not smooth, but verrucose-punctate or rugulose-ridged, at least in scanning electron microscope; stipe with lecythiform caulocystidia or a mixture of lecythiform and non-lecythiform elements $$s"Sect. Ochromarasmius"
3,4 $ Spore surface smooth, even in scanning electron microscope 

4,0 $ Spores coarsely tuberculous, cruciform or almost triangular, with distinct germpore; stipitipellis consisting of non-lecythiform elements $$s"Sect. Nodulososporae"
4,0,N$/// Sect. Nodulososporae (extra-European)
4,5 $ Spores without tubercles, ellipsoid, amygdaliform, subcylindrical, rarely mitriform or hexagonal

5,cs8 $ Veil present as volva, volva-like zone at stipe base or as fringes at pileus margin $$s"Sect. Singerella"
5,6 $ Veil absent, even young

6,0 $ Pileipellis consisting of spheropedunculate and fusiform, partly rostrate elements $$s"Sect. Obscurae"
6,0,N$/// Sect. Obscurae (extra-European)
6,7 $ Pileipellis only consisting of spheropedunculate to vesiculous elements; pileocystidia present or absent

7,8 $ Pseudoparaphyses present, mature lamellae mostly deliquescent; pileus margin slightly to distinctly crenate, stipe often white, rarely pigmented
7,9 $ Pseudoparaphyses absent, lamellae not deliquescent, pileus margin not crenate, but often translucently striate

8,cs4 $ Caulocystidia piliform, cylindrical, fusiform to ellipsoid, not lecythiform $$s"Sect. Candidae"
8,cs5 $ Caulocystidia mostly lecythiform $$s"Sect. Inopinatae"


9,cs1 $ Caulocystidia mostly lecythiform, at stipe apex partly mixed with sorne piliform or non-Iecythiform elements $$s"Sect. Conocybe"
9,10 $ Caulocystidia mostly non-Iecythiform or a mixture of lecythiform, piliform, ellipsoid to fusiform elements

10,cs3 $ Caulocystidia mostly non-Iecythiform, also pilifonn, ellipsoid to fusiform; at stipe apex sometimes few lecythiform elements present $$s"Sect. Pilosellae"
10,cs2 $ Stipitipellis a mixture of lecythiform, piliform, ellipsoid to fusiform elements, the proportion of lecythiform elements ca 25-75 % $$s"Sect. Mixtae"



